            Does this make beef protein useless? No. Collagen-rich protein still counts toward your daily protein total, and the small trials that compared beef protein isolate with whey, discussed below, found similar lean mass gains when people took enough of it alongside training. What it means is that gram for gram, a collagen-heavy beef isolate is a weaker single-shake muscle stimulus than whey, so you dose it higher, pair it with a leucine-rich meal, or accept that you are buying it for dairy avoidance rather than optimal muscle building. If joint and skin support is your real goal, a dedicated <a href="/best-collagen-protein-powder/">collagen protein powder</a> or <a href="/best-bone-broth-protein-powder/">bone broth protein</a> is usually cheaper.
